PROJECT 1: PAPER GLIDER FLIGHT EXPERIMENT
Name: Samuel David 
Date started: September 19th 2026

Project: Paper Glider Flight Experiment
Objective: To investigate how paper-aircraft design affects flight performance.
EXPERIMENT 1 — GLIDER A
Prototype
Name: Glider A — Dart Design

Objective
To build and test a simple paper glider and observe its ability to fly.

Materials
A4 paper
Tape
Paper clip

Design
I made a narrow, dart-shaped paper glider with relatively small wings.
Procedure
Folded the paper into the dart-shaped aircraft.
Tested the glider by throwing it forward.
Observed its flight.
Repeated the test after making small adjustments.

Observation
The glider did not glide successfully. During the launch, the folds opened and the aircraft lost its shape and fell rather than maintaining a stable flight.
Problems identified
The folds were not sufficiently secure.
The wings had limited lifting area.
The aircraft was not sufficiently stable.

Result
UNSUCCESSFUL ❌

What I learned
I learned that an aircraft needs a stable structure and sufficient wing area to generate and maintain lift. A design that looks aerodynamic does not necessarily mean it will glide well.
Improvement for next prototype
I decided to design a glider with larger and more stable wings.
